"Boudewijn Waijers" <kroisos@REMOVETHIS.home.nl> wrote:
>Bruce, cunningly disguised as solomon@gehennom.net wrote:
>
>> To me, the latter is where #naming of gems to catch curses fits in.
>
>> There's really no solution that's not punitive or inconsistent.  Still,
>> it's obviously a case of twisting the game mechanics in a direction they
>> weren't designed to go for the benefit of the player.  It's abusive.
>
>Actually, there is a simple solution that I submitted to the Dev Team (as
>a suggestion, not as a patch).
>
>Just change the way cursing works to a flat chance (say, 15%) of being
>cursed for every single item in your inventory. This way it won't help at
>all to carry 52 items: you'll just get more items cursed.

Sounds like a reasonable idea.  Let's see...
  weapon
  shield or second weapon
  pickaxe
  unicorn horn
  lamp
  helm
  cloak
  body armour
  shirt
  boots
  gloves
  ring #1
  ring #2
  amulet
  wand of teleport (so that it's immediately handy for dealing with
     tentacularities and other such gribblies)
  wand of death (so that it's immediately handy for saying "Rodney, you
     plonker!")
  luckstone
  bag of holding
  reserve bag (sack or oilskin sack) containing items to deal with a
     cursed bag of holding
  possibly a quest artifact
  Book of the Dead
  Bell of Opening
  Candelabrum of Invocation

OK, that's 23 items.  Of those, there are only seven whose status is
likely to be irrelevant (reserve bag, body armour, shirt, helm, boots,
cloak, quest artifact; lamp state doesn't matter *much*, but relighting
a cursed lamp after getting vortexed is a pain; yes, a lamp *is* useful
in the endgame).  So, call it 16 things you care about, and 7 you don't,
becoming 13/8 after you've ditched the invocation items and collected
the amulet, unless you're planning to use the hotter/colder interface
to find the portals.

On average, without defences, you'd get 2.40 (1.95) items you cared about
receiving a cursing step on each cursing, and have a 7% (12%) chance of
having none of your items you care about cursed.  However, no character
fit to ascend is defenceless against cursing.

We'll apply the MR/HSPDAM corrections in a similar way to the current
mechanism; if you have MR or HSPDAM, you get half as much stuff cursed
(7.5%), and if you have both you get one-third as much stuff cursed (5%).

This gives an ascension-worthy valkyrie a 44% (or 51%, once she's got
the amulet) chance of having nothing she cares about hit by the curse,
regardless of what she's carrying, and a 31% (34% once she's got the
amulet) chance of having *nothing at all* cursed, if she goes with the
spartan-pack strategy.

By contrast, a valkyrie with a full pack, under the current system, has
a 34% chance of having something she cares about cursed; a valkyrie with
the spartan pack described above (carrying the amulet rather than the
invocation items) has a 74% chance. Furthermore, she has *no* chance of
getting away with nothing cursed.

(This whole analysis assumes the absence of Magicbane, but that's just
because, well, MB makes the curse spell look feeble anyway :)

Obviously the percentage could be tweaked - but there's probably not
*that* much slack in it, really.

What would be *really* nice is a mechanism that *penalises*
packstuffing.

